        You slam your hands down on the table hard enough to rattle the lunch trays, springing to your feet as righteous anger flows through you. You snap at the bullies, glaring at them as you tell them off for making fun of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Mata</span>. They’re just mad that they’re boring and uncultured and that their mothers don’t love them enough to make them a lunch half as good as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Mata</span>’s! <br>
        <br>
        This may be going a bit too far, as you realize everyone is staring at you with a surprised expression. Yelling that out may have been a bit much, <span style="color:LightCoral">but it seems to work as the main kid laughing turns red and mumbles out <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“whatever!”</span> before quickly grabbing his lunch and moving to another table, followed by his friends.</span> Eventually, everyone returns to their lunch, and you sit back down blushing yourself from causing such a scene. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“…Thank you.”</span> You hear <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Mata</span> whisper. You glance at him and see him giving you a genuine, cute smile, his voice full of something heavy and raw. <span style="color:Pink">Your blush deepens as you chuckle, rubbing the back of your head and telling him it was nothing. You can’t stand bullies like that and had to say something. As long as you’re here, he has nothing to worry about!</span> <br>
        <br>

         <<set _ad to [
